---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
import Opinion from '../../components/site/Opinion.astro';
---
<Journey chapter="lead" first="roles" title="A lead" description="One agent plans, writes briefs, reviews and merges, and the others build. The lead's window holds reports, not the work.">
  <Step id="roles" title="One plans, the others build">
    <p>Now <a href={url('journey/parallel/')}>the coordinating agent from step 7</a> stops writing code. As the lead, it writes briefs, hands them out, and collects what comes back.</p>
    <Opinion date="2026-11-18">
      <p>Claude is better at design, and the current class of Fable 5.2 and Opus 5.5 is better at high-level decisions. That is what I put in the lead’s seat.</p>
    </Opinion>
  </Step>
  <Step id="shapes" title="Other ways to split one job">
    <p>Try four ways to route the same request. The shaded agent runs a different model, so whoever judges the work is never the one who built it.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="shape" data-val="pair" data-default aria-pressed="true">Build, then review</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="shape" data-val="line" aria-pressed="false">Plan, build, review</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="shape" data-val="best" aria-pressed="false">Two builds, keep one</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="shape" data-val="fan" aria-pressed="false">Fan out</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="gate" title="A check before main">
    <p>Move <a href={url('journey/check/')}>the check from step 5</a> right in front of main. Nothing a builder finishes lands until it passes.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="on" data-default aria-pressed="true">With the check</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="off" aria-pressed="false">Without</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A rule for the lead">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="What the lead does before a merge">{`Before you merge a builder's branch into main: run the tests on that branch and open the page it changed.
If either fails, send it back to the same builder with the output.
Do not fix it yourself, and do not merge to make the queue shorter.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="reports" title="What the lead reads">
    <p>If every builder sends back everything it did, the lead’s window quickly fills up with other agents’ noise.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="short" data-val="all" data-default aria-pressed="true">Everything</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="short" data-val="short" aria-pressed="false">Short reports</button>
    </div>
    <More title="What to ask builders for">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="A short report">{`Report in five lines: what you changed, how you checked it, what you did not check, anything I have to decide.
Do not paste the diff or the logs. I will open them if I need them.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
    <Next from="lead" more={[{ href: 'explain/orchestration/', text: 'Ways to split work' }, { href: 'models/', text: 'Which model where' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The tasks, handoffs, and window percentages above are illustrative examples.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
